This repository contains work from two sources. They are kept in separate directories.

1. OAI/ : the formalisation by the paper's authors

   The directory OAI/ holds files from the repository "openai/math",
   https://github.com/openai/math, at commit
   fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb, which is licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0. They are the 288 files that make up the import closure of the module
   OAI.Combinatorics.HadwigerCounterexample.Main:

     OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerCounterexample/   276 files
     OAI/Combinatorics/HadwigerMatching/          10 files
     OAI/Combinatorics/ListHadwiger/               2 files (Basic.lean, Model.lean)

   They formalise the paper "A counterexample to Hadwiger's conjecture" (OpenAI,
   23 September 2026). The proof of the paper's main theorem (Theorem 1.1) that this
   repository relies on is that formalisation. It is the work of its authors, not of this
   repository.

   State of the files: copied byte for byte. Each file has the git blob hash it has in
   the upstream tree at the commit above. If a later commit of this repository changes any
   of them (for example to port them to Lean's module system or to a newer Lean and
   Mathlib), that commit and the file docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md say so, as section 4(b) of
   the licence requires.

   The upstream repository has no NOTICE file and the files carry no copyright headers.

2. Hadwiger/ : this project

   The directory Hadwiger/ is this project's own development: its definitions and
   statements (minors and the Hadwiger number, connected matchings, fractional colourings),
   its proofs of Proposition 3.5, of the bounds of Section 1, of Corollary 1.2 in its
   fractional-chromatic form from Theorem 1.1, of Lemma 2.2, Lemma 3.2 and Lemma 3.3, and
   the file Hadwiger/UpstreamBridge.lean, which carries the upstream theorem over to this
   project's statement of Theorem 1.1.

The paper itself is not stored in this repository; docs/PROVENANCE.md records where it is.
